      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I use a standard xbox one controller for pc, paired with a headset (no motion controllers). Before the only bugs was that I had to press esc on my keyboard to open the regular menu and I couldn't access the new av3 menu at all ('R' did open the av3 menu but I couldn't do anything on it).\nNow it won't even take the analogue inputs.\nAs for the person above comment about desktop not being able to rotate objects, using 'i', 'j', 'k', 'L' as you would 'w', 'a', 's', 'd', does as you described (also mouse wheel to move in and out, and 'u' and 'o' for the other axis)",
